WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.134 --> 00:00:13.732
The origin of April Fool's Day dates back so long ago that it is not clear when or how it got started.

2
00:00:13.733 --> 00:00:21.858
Some people say the day for fooling began in France when a king agreed to change the yearly calendar.

3
00:00:21.859 --> 00:00:26.626
He moved New Year's Day from April 1 to January 1.

4
00:00:26.627 --> 00:00:33.657
It was difficult to communicate in those days, so many people did not hear about the change.

5
00:00:33.658 --> 00:00:38.599
Some people continued to celebrate New Year's Day on April 1.

6
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.783
These people were called April Fools.

7
00:00:41.784 --> 00:00:47.421
When the king announced the new calendar, the neighbors in one village discussed it.

8
00:00:47.422 --> 00:00:52.289
"Hey, did you hear that we have a new calendar?" said one.

9
00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:57.057
"Yes, New Year's Day does not fall on April 1 anymore.

10
00:00:57.058 --> 00:01:01.892
Now, it is on January 1," said the other.

11
00:01:01.893 --> 00:01:06.496
"Now we have to celebrate New Year's Day in January when it is cold."

12
00:01:06.497 --> 00:01:11.814
"That's right. By the way, do you think Louis knows about this?"

13
00:01:11.815 --> 00:01:15.550
"The whole village knows, but Louis will not accept it.

14
00:01:15.551 --> 00:01:18.508
As you know, he is a stubborn man."

15
00:01:18.509 --> 00:01:21.860
Louis always insisted on being right.

16
00:01:21.861 --> 00:01:27.540
He did not listen very well to others, and his neighbors did not like him.

17
00:01:27.541 --> 00:01:29.900
"Louis always thinks that he is right."

18
00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:35.386
"Yes, he does. Even when he is wrong, he never admits it," they said.

19
00:01:35.387 --> 00:01:43.463
When Louis walked by, they called out, "Hey, Louis! Do you know we have to celebrate New Year's Day on January 1?"

20
00:01:43.464 --> 00:01:48.036
"Ha-ha! You believe that rumor?" Louis laughed.

21
00:01:48.037 --> 00:01:53.419
"We always celebrate the New Year on April 1. You are so foolish!"

22
00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:57.820
His neighbors decided this was a chance to play a trick on him.

23
00:01:57.821 --> 00:02:02.121
"Ha-ha! This is going to be fun!" they laughed.

24
00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:06.678
The next day, Louis' neighbor called him into his house.

25
00:02:06.679 --> 00:02:09.228
"Hey Louis, will you do me a favor?"

26
00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:11.849
"If I can," Louis said.

27
00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:20.236
"Look, I broke my leg," said his neighbor, "so I cannot deliver this important message to the lord of the next village.

28
00:02:20.237 --> 00:02:22.536
Will you take it for me?"

29
00:02:22.537 --> 00:02:25.656
"I have work to do," said Louis.

30
00:02:25.657 --> 00:02:32.418
"But it is not far to the next village, so I'll do it. But just this once!"

31
00:02:32.419 --> 00:02:36.953
Louis went to the next village and knocked at the door of the lord.

32
00:02:36.954 --> 00:02:42.514
"Hi, this letter is from our village," he said when a servant answered.

33
00:02:42.515 --> 00:02:49.734
The servant read the letter and laughed. "Interesting! But I am sorry.

34
00:02:49.735 --> 00:02:52.867
This letter is not for the lord of this village.

35
00:02:52.868 --> 00:02:56.854
Would you deliver this to the lord in the next village?"

36
00:02:56.855 --> 00:02:59.773
So Louis went to the next village.

37
00:02:59.774 --> 00:03:03.918
The servant of the lord of that village also laughed when he read it.

38
00:03:03.919 --> 00:03:07.017
"Thank you, but this letter is not for my master.

39
00:03:07.018 --> 00:03:10.754
Please take it over to the lord of the next village."

40
00:03:10.755 --> 00:03:13.410
Louis thought this was very strange.

41
00:03:13.411 --> 00:03:19.251
"Didn't my friend know the right village to send this letter to?" he wondered.

42
00:03:19.252 --> 00:03:24.028
"The next village is too far away. I think that I have walked far enough!

43
00:03:24.029 --> 00:03:27.959
My friend must be wrong! I will return the letter to him."

44
00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:31.902
So Louis returned home. He was very tired.

45
00:03:31.903 --> 00:03:38.241
He sat at his table and thought, "Hmm, why did everyone laugh when they read this letter?"

46
00:03:38.242 --> 00:03:40.852
Out of curiosity, he opened it.

47
00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:48.160
The letter said: The new calendar moved New Year's Day from April 1 to January 1.

48
00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:53.673
But I will celebrate New Year's Day on April 1 because I refuse to change.

49
00:03:53.674 --> 00:04:00.110
I am an April Fool. Please send me to the lord of the next village.
